The Angband world calls this "Ironman" play.  If you enable the
Ironman limit in Angband, you can only go downward - never back up.

I don't know which game is more challenging in Ironman mode.  In
Angband, there are only shops on the top level, so if you Ironman, you
can shop once and then never again.  However, Angband's levels are
3-4x times bigger than NetHack's so there's more change to find
things.

In Angband, there are no dungeon branches like Sokoban or the Mines.
I suppose you could make Sokoban and the Mines "only once" for each
level.  Having to skip both would be much harder.



